# Orbit Sakshi is an evidence repository. The bytes ARE the product.
#
# Git's end-of-line normalisation rewrites CRLF to LF on commit. For source
# code that is a convenience; here it is corruption — the receipt chain
# commits to the exact bytes as pulled from CelesTrak, and a rewritten byte
# breaks the hash. On 2026-08-09 this silently mutated six evidence files in
# transport: a fresh `git clone` verified as FAIL ("Do not trust this copy")
# while the identical tree on the live site verified PASS.
#
# `-text` disables all EOL conversion. Nothing in this repository is ever
# normalised on commit or checkout. Recorded on-chain.

* -text
